docs_content = """# 6-DoF Rigid-Body Equations of Motion
1. Coordinate Frames
 * Inertial Frame (\mathcal{F}_I): North-East-Down (NED) local tangent plane.
 * Body-Fixed Frame (\mathcal{F}_B): Origin at the vehicle Center of Gravity (CG), x_b forward along the fuselage centerline, y_b right wing, z_b downward.
2. State Vector
The 13-element state vector is defined as:

where:
 * (x, y, z): Inertial NED position [\text{m}]
 * (u, v, w): Body-frame linear velocity components [\text{m/s}]
 * (q_0, q_1, q_2, q_3): Attitude unit quaternion (q_0 scalar part)
 * (p, q, r): Body-frame roll, pitch, and yaw angular rates [\text{rad/s}]
3. Aerodynamic Forces & Moments
Dynamic pressure is computed as \bar{q} = \frac{1}{2} \rho V^2, where V = \sqrt{u^2 + v^2 + w^2}.
Angle of attack \alpha = \arctan2(w, u) and sideslip angle \beta = \arcsin(v / V).
 * Lift Coefficient: C_L = C_{L0} + C_{L\alpha} \alpha
 * Drag Coefficient: C_D = C_{D0} + k C_L^2
 * Pitching Moment Coefficient: C_m = C_{m0} + C_{m\alpha} \alpha + C_{mq} \frac{q \bar{c}}{2V}
   """
